The "game in progress under your name" is the game that crashed. This
happens because slash'em is detecting the files that go with its levels
in /var/games/slashem.

should slash'em handle these things just like vanilla, so there should
be a recover program to go with it (/usr/lib/games/slashem/recover,
probably). Just run it on the ${UID}charname.0 file in
/var/games/slashem. hopefully, that'll work. On the other hand, my
personal experience is that it doesn't (on my system, in vanilla), as I
lack permission to do write the save file. In the case that fails, do
the following beforehand:

sudo touch /var/games/slashem/save/${UID}charname
sudo chown ${USER}:games /var/games/slashem/save/${UID}charname

should your system not be sudo-enabled, just do su instead, and run
those commands minus the sudo.

note that chowning ${USER}:games pressuposes that's what slash'em
expects. Try creating another savefile and checking its ownership if
you're not sure



